<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs mixed as the Dow makes further progress.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs mixed as the Dow makes further progress.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were mixed in late New York trade, where the Dow Industrials were 19.63 points higher at 6,965 at 7.45 a.m. NZT.</p>
<p>There was heavy volume in both Tranz Rail and Thistle Hotels.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$28 1/8	 -0 1/2 *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$26 3/4	 +0 5/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$20 1/2	 +0 1/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$14 1/4	 nil    *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$74 1/4	 +0 1/4 *</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$17 3/4	 nil    *</p>
<p>Thistle	  London  199 1/2	   -2 1/2</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  36		  +0 1/2</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  250 1/2	   nil</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  161 1/4	   +3 3/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  148 1/2	   -0 1/2</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.24	    nil</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.60	    +2</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$2.31	    -5</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
